From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: sites are told the engine is Google Chrome

A Chromium build sends no browser brand in `navigator.userAgentData` or
`Sec-CH-UA`, only `Chromium` and a GREASE brand. Akamai's bot check
refuses that on some sites: Citi's sign-in answers "Access Denied" to
stock Chromium and lets Google Chrome through.

GetUserAgentBrandList now always adds `Google Chrome`, as a Chrome build
does. The User-Agent string is unchanged: Chrome's and Chromium's are the
same.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`. guard-browser-brand.sh checks it.
---
 components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
index 8332938..1d8f36a 100644
--- a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
+++ b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
@@ -158,10 +158,9 @@ const blink::UserAgentBrandList GetUserAgentBrandList(
   int major_version_number;
   bool parse_result = base::StringToInt(major_version, &major_version_number);
   DCHECK(parse_result);
-  std::optional<std::string> brand;
-#if !BUILDFLAG(CHROMIUM_BRANDING)
-  brand = version_info::GetProductName();
-#endif
+  // Domicile: send Chrome's brand. A Chromium build sends none, and Akamai's
+  // bot check refuses that on some sites' sign-ins and lets Chrome through.
+  std::optional<std::string> brand = "Google Chrome";
 
   std::string brand_version =
       output_version_type == blink::UserAgentBrandVersionType::kFullVersion
